  "query_preview": "..\nShallow fog is possible again, especially in low lying areas and \nin river basins. A light west wind tonight will most likely keep \nthe fog at bay. Any fog that forms will erode quickly as a weak \nfront moves through early this morning.\n\nUpper ridging looks to rebound with dry weather conditions and \nwarming temperatures through the beginning of the week. Highs \nacross NE Montana for Sunday will reach into the 50s and 60s. This\nwill be short lived however, as the next cold front will bring in\nbreezy conditions Sunday night and cooler temperatures for \nMonday. As quickly as it left, ridging aloft then builds back in \nfor mid week returning highs in in the 60s Wednesday and Thursday. \n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS:\n\nSlight edits to visibility using RRFS for low confidence shallow\nfog. No changes to NBM otherwise.",
